{"requirements":[{"id":"local-account","requirement":"Create a local account named opsadmin on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The baseline showed opsadmin absent. The executor then created it, and direct passwd/identity checks confirmed the local account both before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1f4940c64b424a63","cmd-44ef6a86a6554b8e","cmd-77e499540b01410f","cmd-19ae75d9dbb543df"]},{"id":"private-home","requirement":"Give opsadmin a private home directory.","status":"satisfied","summary":"/home/opsadmin is a directory owned by opsadmin:opsadmin with exact mode 0700; owner read, write, and execute access was also tested after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-145082bad9a047a4","cmd-77e499540b01410f","cmd-19ae75d9dbb543df"]},{"id":"administrative-privileges","requirement":"Grant opsadmin full administrative privileges.","status":"satisfied","summary":"opsadmin belongs to wheel, sudo policy authorizes (ALL) ALL, and an authenticated sudo command executed as opsadmin directly returned UID 0.","evidence_ids":["cmd-44ef6a86a6554b8e","cmd-145082bad9a047a4","cmd-19ae75d9dbb543df"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The account, group, ownership, permission, SELinux-label, and credential changes in cmd-44ef6a86a6554b8e directly implemented the task. The only other state-changing action, cmd-8bb43a9590284339, initiated the required provider restart and left no adverse residue. Afterward there were no failed services, package health remained good, and listening services recovered; temporary-file differences were ordinary reboot-generated systemd private directories.","evidence_ids":["cmd-44ef6a86a6554b8e","cmd-8bb43a9590284339","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All public task outcomes are satisfied. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete: node1 was healthy before restart, acknowledged the restart, changed boot identity, and returned running with zero failed units and the requested account, home, and sudo state intact. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":[]}
